            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="TOW03" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Joseph Lomas</forename>
                        <surname>Towers</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1770-04-18">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1831-10-04"/>
                    <occupation>Unitarian preacherLibrarian and book colector</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>The only son of <persName key="TOW01">Joseph Towers</persName>.
     Early entries are coded for Joseph senr who dies in 1799. There is an entry for Joseph junr in 1798, and this and subsequent 
     entries have been coded for Towers' son Joseph Lomas Towers (<title>DNB</title>) (1770-1831)</p>
                        <p> There are a very few entries which could be ambiguous between John Towers <title>DNB</title>, Joseph senr's brother, and 
    Joseph Lomas Towers, before the  former's death in 1804.  But Godwin indicates Towers Junr in 1798 and all those 
    entries subsequent to this have been coded as Joseph junr .</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other"><title>DNB</title>.</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
